## What I actually took away from this

The student in this case had "heard about UPI scams" before. That's the frustrating part. Awareness alone clearly isn't enough. In the moment — phone call, social pressure, a real UPI notification on screen — the knowledge didn't kick in fast enough.

That's the real lesson I took from this. Knowing that scams exist and knowing exactly how they work are two different things. And even knowing how they work isn't enough if you've never thought through what you would actually do in that moment.

Proper digital literacy isn't just information. It's internalised habits. The habit here is one sentence: *"I never need a PIN to receive money."* If that's automatic, the scam fails every time.

